# One ignore file for every image, because every build in this repository uses the repository root
# as its context (see the docker build commands in the Dockerfile headers). Keeping the context
# small is not cosmetic: everything listed here would otherwise be uploaded to the builder on every
# build, and a stale node_modules or .venv copied into a stage would shadow the locked install.

# Version control and editor state
.git
.gitignore
.github

# Governance and generated agent files: never needed inside an image
.eep
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md

# Container definitions themselves, except docker/, which frontend.Dockerfile copies nginx.conf from
docker-compose*.yaml
docker-compose*.yml
.dockerignore

# Python component
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.coverage
**/htmlcov

# Node components: the lockfile is copied explicitly, an installed tree never is
**/node_modules
**/npm-debug.log*
**/.vite
**/coverage

# Build output produced inside the builder stage, never carried in from the host
**/dist
**/build

# Local environment files: configuration reaches a container as environment, not as a baked layer
**/.env
**/.env.*

# Editor and operating system noise
**/.DS_Store
**/.idea
**/.vscode
